# The fixture filesystem df's and quot's b6sim cases report on -- task C4a.
#
# NOT AN IMAGE ANYTHING BOOTS.  It exists because df(1) and quot(1) read a FILESYSTEM, and
# a flat b6fsutil image is an ordinary host file, so those two are the first programs here
# that can be tested under b6sim against real on-disk structure rather than only for their
# argument handling.  ../../ls/README.md's limitation -- b6sim cannot read a directory --
# is what keeps du(1) out of that world; neither of these reads one.
#
# ../../../root.manifest is the real one and this is deliberately nothing like it: no
# device nodes (b6fsutil needs no kernel to make them, but nothing here looks at one), no
# programs, and 200 blocks rather than 2000.  What it has instead is FILE SIZES CHOSEN FOR
# THE ARITHMETIC, since a block is 3072 bytes and every number both programs print is a
# division by it:
#
#   /small       64 bytes -- well inside one block
#   /mid       3072 bytes -- EXACTLY one block, the off-by-one either program could make
#   /big       9216 bytes -- three blocks, and DELIBERATELY still direct: NADDR is 8 with
#                            six direct, and an indirect block is one quot does not count,
#                            di_size being what it divides.  That gap is icheck(1)'s
#                            question, task C4e, and this fixture does not prejudge it
#   /other     1536 bytes -- half a block
#   /d/nested   128 bytes -- and a directory to reach it through
#
# THE THREE OWNERS ARE THE POINT OF THE quot CASES.  0 is root, which is uid 0 on every
# host that has ever run this build, so `quot' may print the name.  201 and 202 are in no
# host /etc/passwd, so quot's `#%d' fallback prints the number -- which is the only way a
# per-uid report can be diffed under a harness whose getpwent(3) reads THE BUILD MACHINE's
# password file.  cmd/quot/test/CMakeLists.txt says the same thing from the other end.
#
# The sources are generated at configure time into fsimg.d/ by CMakeLists.txt beside this
# file -- they are runs of one 64-byte line, so nothing binary is checked in -- and the
# paths below resolve against b6fsutil's WORKING_DIRECTORY, which is the test's build
# directory, exactly as ../../../root.manifest's resolve against kernel/test's.

default
owner 0
group 0
dirmode 0755
filemode 0644

dir /d

file /small
source fsimg.d/small

file /mid
owner 201
source fsimg.d/mid

file /big
owner 201
source fsimg.d/big

file /other
owner 202
source fsimg.d/other

file /d/nested
owner 202
source fsimg.d/nested
